<!-- Part 14 e2e scenario 5/5 (most complex, and the actual point of the whole
     exercise): a genuinely CONTRADICTORY override that a DL reasoner (HermiT)
     should be able to flag as unsatisfiable.

     BaseType declares Mandatory "Signal" : PropertyType/Double with
     ValueRank=1 (OneDimension, a 1-D array). SubType <: BaseType overrides
     "Signal" with ValueRank=2 (2-D array, collapsed into the
     ValueRank_MoreDimensions symbolic class).

     ValueRank_OneDimension and ValueRank_MoreDimensions are declared pairwise
     disjoint (semantic_bridge_to_owl.md §17, plus the disjointness added in
     lib/owlbuilder.py precisely so a reasoner can catch exactly this).
     VT(SubType, "Signal") ends up asserted as BOTH:
       - rdfs:subClassOf ValueRank_MoreDimensions  (§8/§17, its own overridden ValueRank)
       - rdfs:subClassOf VT(BaseType, "Signal")     (§9, itself subClassOf ValueRank_OneDimension)
     i.e. simultaneously OneDimension and MoreDimensions, unsatisfiable.
     This test only checks the structural precondition (both disjoint
     ancestors are reachable) since no OWL DL reasoner is available in this
     environment; see semanticbridge2owl.py's module docstring for how to
     confirm it with Protégé/HermiT. -->
